1
00:00:03,962 --> 00:00:06,923
<i>[dramatic music]</i>

2
00:00:06,923 --> 00:00:14,014
<i>♪ ♪</i>

3
00:01:26,628 --> 00:01:29,547
<i>[suspenseful music]</i>

4
00:01:29,547 --> 00:01:35,136
<i>♪ ♪</i>

5
00:01:35,136 --> 00:01:38,598
Oh, fuck. Fuck!

6
00:01:38,598 --> 00:01:44,729
<i>♪ ♪</i>

7
00:01:45,814 --> 00:01:47,148
Are you sure it's him?

8
00:01:47,148 --> 00:01:49,025
<i>I saw him hit the pavement.</i>

9
00:01:49,025 --> 00:01:51,736
Maruyama-san,
before Nakahara fell,

10
00:01:51,736 --> 00:01:54,155
I saw Tozawa enter
the building.

11
00:01:54,155 --> 00:01:55,990
Do you have photos of that?

12
00:01:55,990 --> 00:01:58,159
No. But he was there.

13
00:02:00,620 --> 00:02:03,748
Fine.
We'll include that detail.

14
00:02:03,748 --> 00:02:05,291
Start dictating.

15
00:02:05,291 --> 00:02:08,420
[both speaking Japanese]

16
00:02:13,383 --> 00:02:15,093
Answer me.

17
00:02:15,093 --> 00:02:17,387
What were you looking for
in my study?

18
00:02:17,387 --> 00:02:18,930
Nothing.

19
00:02:18,930 --> 00:02:21,766
I was curious to see
where you live, where you work.

20
00:02:23,935 --> 00:02:25,603
Don't lie to me.

21
00:02:25,603 --> 00:02:26,938
I'm not lying to you.

22
00:02:26,938 --> 00:02:27,939
I'm not a stupid man.

23
00:02:27,939 --> 00:02:30,233
I'm not--
come on, I was just--

24
00:02:30,233 --> 00:02:31,735
oh, okay.

25
00:02:31,735 --> 00:02:34,195
What the fuck?

26
00:02:40,577 --> 00:02:42,579
What's on this?

27
00:02:42,579 --> 00:02:46,708
Did you photograph
my blueprints?

28
00:02:46,708 --> 00:02:50,962
[sighs] I don't understand.

29
00:02:50,962 --> 00:02:53,048
What use is my work to you?

30
00:02:53,048 --> 00:02:55,925
<i>[soft dramatic music]</i>

31
00:02:55,925 --> 00:02:59,429
My club is half-owned
by the Yakuza.

32
00:02:59,429 --> 00:03:01,431
They found out
about your project.

33
00:03:01,431 --> 00:03:03,141
They asked me
to get the information.

34
00:03:03,141 --> 00:03:07,604
I said I would if they give me
the club, free and clear.

35
00:03:07,604 --> 00:03:09,898
So you did it for yourself.

36
00:03:09,898 --> 00:03:11,274
Yes.

37
00:03:11,274 --> 00:03:14,527
And for the girls, too,
to protect them.

38
00:03:14,527 --> 00:03:16,446
I see.

39
00:03:16,446 --> 00:03:18,031
For the girls.

40
00:03:18,031 --> 00:03:21,076
And my career gets ruined
in the process.

41
00:03:22,660 --> 00:03:24,329
You can sleep on the couch.

42
00:03:24,329 --> 00:03:26,915
It's too late
to drive you home.

43
00:03:26,915 --> 00:03:28,792
We'll discuss this tomorrow.

44
00:03:28,792 --> 00:03:35,882
<i>♪ ♪</i>

45
00:03:38,968 --> 00:03:42,013
[sirens wailing]
[indistinct chatter]

46
00:03:42,013 --> 00:03:43,848
[speaking Japanese]

47
00:03:58,738 --> 00:04:00,365
[speaking Japanese

48
00:04:40,113 --> 00:04:43,074
<i>[tense music]</i>

49
00:04:43,074 --> 00:04:46,995
<i>♪ ♪</i>

50
00:04:46,995 --> 00:04:49,998
[breathing heavily]

51
00:04:49,998 --> 00:04:57,088
<i>♪ ♪</i>

52
00:05:08,475 --> 00:05:12,771
[both speaking Japanese

53
00:05:55,522 --> 00:05:56,773
[neck cracks]

54
00:06:03,697 --> 00:06:06,282
[engine whirring]

55
00:06:16,876 --> 00:06:19,921
<i>Oi! Oi! Oi!</i>

56
00:06:29,347 --> 00:06:31,182
[speaking Japanese]

57
00:06:50,827 --> 00:06:53,455
[baby crying]

58
00:06:59,210 --> 00:07:06,217
<i>♪ ♪</i>

59
00:07:20,106 --> 00:07:21,608
Come with me.

60
00:07:43,755 --> 00:07:48,301
Masa-san, I am so sorry.

61
00:07:48,301 --> 00:07:50,804
I won't tell them what I saw.

62
00:07:50,804 --> 00:07:54,057
I'll say you caught me first,
that I couldn't find anything.

63
00:07:54,057 --> 00:07:56,768
Ishida will have
to accept that.

64
00:07:56,768 --> 00:07:58,478
And what if
you do not provide Ishida

65
00:07:58,478 --> 00:08:01,064
with the location?

66
00:08:01,064 --> 00:08:02,399
What will he do to you?

67
00:08:02,399 --> 00:08:04,275
That's not your problem.

68
00:08:04,275 --> 00:08:05,944
I got myself into this mess.

69
00:08:05,944 --> 00:08:07,696
I'll get myself out.

70
00:08:11,366 --> 00:08:14,452
There's another project
I'm working on,

71
00:08:14,452 --> 00:08:17,163
early stages.

72
00:08:17,163 --> 00:08:21,584
If Ishida bought surrounding
properties there instead,

73
00:08:21,584 --> 00:08:24,004
he could make
a significant return.

74
00:08:25,130 --> 00:08:26,756
But you'd still be ruined.

75
00:08:26,756 --> 00:08:28,091
Maybe not.

76
00:08:28,091 --> 00:08:32,220
Unlike Shimbashi,
this one is a private venture.

77
00:08:32,220 --> 00:08:34,597
If there was a run
on nearby real estate,

78
00:08:34,597 --> 00:08:38,852
the owners would profit
and likely ask no questions.

79
00:08:40,228 --> 00:08:42,480
If we convinced Ishida
to accept this,

80
00:08:42,480 --> 00:08:47,110
you could keep your club,
and I could keep my job.

81
00:08:50,238 --> 00:08:52,407
What if I could get
someone I know

82
00:08:52,407 --> 00:08:57,120
to publish the location
of your project in the press?

83
00:08:57,120 --> 00:08:58,288
Wouldn't that make

84
00:08:58,288 --> 00:09:01,750
the Shimbashi information
worthless?

85
00:09:01,750 --> 00:09:05,170
And then I could make
my proposal

86
00:09:05,170 --> 00:09:08,548
of a valuable replacement.

87
00:09:08,548 --> 00:09:10,342
Why are you helping me?

88
00:09:14,220 --> 00:09:17,057
I know what it is
to need forgiveness.

89
00:09:24,522 --> 00:09:26,024
Thank you
for the call last night.

90
00:09:26,024 --> 00:09:28,818
It was smart of you
not to talk to anyone else.

91
00:09:28,818 --> 00:09:31,279
Of course.

92
00:09:31,279 --> 00:09:35,492
You know there's no way
that Nakahara jumped, right?

93
00:09:35,492 --> 00:09:36,993
I just wish
I would have gotten a picture

94
00:09:36,993 --> 00:09:38,370
of Tozawa
entering the building.

95
00:09:38,370 --> 00:09:41,456
That fucker never
came back out.

96
00:09:41,456 --> 00:09:46,044
I will get back to you
with anything we learn.

97
00:09:46,044 --> 00:09:48,213
And by we,
you mean that female detective

98
00:09:48,213 --> 00:09:50,840
who sent me packing
the other day?

99
00:09:50,840 --> 00:09:52,008
How's that working out?

100
00:09:52,008 --> 00:09:55,095
She's, like, your new partner
or something?

101
00:09:57,097 --> 00:09:59,057
It is working fine.

102
00:09:59,057 --> 00:10:00,350
Great.

103
00:10:00,350 --> 00:10:02,227
But we're still a thing, right?

104
00:10:02,227 --> 00:10:04,312
Starsky and Hutch?

105
00:10:04,312 --> 00:10:07,148
Which of us is Starsky?

106
00:10:07,148 --> 00:10:08,775
Me, obviously.

107
00:10:11,903 --> 00:10:13,905
I do not think so.

108
00:10:34,759 --> 00:10:39,639
[both speaking Japanese]

109
00:11:17,177 --> 00:11:19,679
[silverware clatters]

110
00:11:49,167 --> 00:11:51,002
[smacks table]

111
00:11:59,427 --> 00:12:06,476
<i>♪ ♪</i>

112
00:12:15,860 --> 00:12:18,071
- [whispering indistinctly]
- Ah.

113
00:12:33,878 --> 00:12:36,214
[whispering indistinctly]

114
00:12:40,969 --> 00:12:44,431
[speaking Japanese

115
00:12:52,772 --> 00:12:54,232
<i>all: Hai.</i>

116
00:12:54,232 --> 00:12:55,942
[speaking Japanese

117
00:13:00,155 --> 00:13:03,199
[phone buzzing]

118
00:13:08,580 --> 00:13:11,583
[speaking Japanese

119
00:13:46,659 --> 00:13:49,287
[door slams]

120
00:14:48,513 --> 00:14:51,516
[indistinct chatter]

121
00:15:00,191 --> 00:15:03,194
[both speaking Japanese

122
00:16:18,895 --> 00:16:21,022
And it's for sure that
this complex is being built

123
00:16:21,022 --> 00:16:22,440
over Shimbashi Station?

124
00:16:22,440 --> 00:16:24,442
Yep, I've seen
the blueprints.

125
00:16:24,442 --> 00:16:25,902
It won't be announced
for a good year,

126
00:16:25,902 --> 00:16:27,529
but that's where it's going.

127
00:16:27,529 --> 00:16:29,072
This anything to do
with Ishida?

128
00:16:29,072 --> 00:16:31,866
Can you just do this for me?

129
00:16:31,866 --> 00:16:33,118
Are you in trouble?

130
00:16:37,497 --> 00:16:39,082
Fine.

131
00:16:39,082 --> 00:16:41,459
I'll follow it up.
[glass shatters]

132
00:16:41,459 --> 00:16:43,378
[speaking Japanese

133
00:16:49,968 --> 00:16:51,970
What's up with you?

134
00:16:51,970 --> 00:16:55,223
There's something
I need to tell you.

135
00:16:55,223 --> 00:16:56,975
Tozawa's back in Tokyo.

136
00:16:56,975 --> 00:16:58,768
I saw him
at his lawyer's office,

137
00:16:58,768 --> 00:17:02,147
and I followed him to a medical
building in Minato-ku.

138
00:17:02,147 --> 00:17:04,149
I'm gonna make him pay
for what he did.

139
00:17:04,149 --> 00:17:06,776
I'm not giving up.

140
00:17:06,776 --> 00:17:08,820
Jake, I love you
for wanting to take him on,

141
00:17:08,820 --> 00:17:12,407
but having a death wish
isn't sexy.

142
00:17:12,407 --> 00:17:15,910
We had videotape
of his men killing Pol--

143
00:17:15,910 --> 00:17:18,079
no consequences.

144
00:17:18,079 --> 00:17:21,791
His men beat you up--
no consequences.

145
00:17:21,791 --> 00:17:23,668
So no, I'd rather not
find out one day

146
00:17:23,668 --> 00:17:24,878
that you just disappeared,

147
00:17:24,878 --> 00:17:26,588
and there will be
no consequences.

148
00:17:26,588 --> 00:17:30,842
<i>♪ ♪</i>

149
00:17:30,842 --> 00:17:33,845
[grunting]

150
00:17:33,845 --> 00:17:40,935
<i>♪ ♪</i>

151
00:17:43,688 --> 00:17:46,775
[sighs]

152
00:17:46,775 --> 00:17:53,865
<i>♪ ♪</i>

153
00:18:10,715 --> 00:18:12,884
[speaking Japanese

154
00:18:41,037 --> 00:18:42,747
[chuckles]

155
00:19:26,499 --> 00:19:28,460
[both laugh]

156
00:19:37,802 --> 00:19:39,637
They know the actual location

157
00:19:39,637 --> 00:19:41,389
of where the project is
being built?

158
00:19:41,389 --> 00:19:42,682
Yeah, my source
just called me.

159
00:19:42,682 --> 00:19:44,184
They said Shimbashi.

160
00:19:44,184 --> 00:19:46,644
Are they in
the transport office?

161
00:19:46,644 --> 00:19:49,731
No, they're...
in a different field,

162
00:19:49,731 --> 00:19:51,983
but I trust them.

163
00:19:54,652 --> 00:19:58,281
Maruyama-san?

164
00:19:58,281 --> 00:20:00,700
Have the article ready
for tomorrow's edition.

165
00:20:03,244 --> 00:20:07,624
I was thinking...
Kurihira should do it.

166
00:20:07,624 --> 00:20:10,168
You want to give away
your scoop?

167
00:20:10,168 --> 00:20:12,170
I think
he could really use it.

168
00:20:12,170 --> 00:20:14,506
You know, Baku's been
riding him really hard.

169
00:20:16,174 --> 00:20:18,343
Fine.

170
00:20:18,343 --> 00:20:23,640
Oh, and your request for your
trip to America was approved.

171
00:20:23,640 --> 00:20:24,849
Oh.

172
00:20:24,849 --> 00:20:26,851
Oh, I'm just not sure,
what with everything going on,

173
00:20:26,851 --> 00:20:28,603
that I should go, you know...

174
00:20:28,603 --> 00:20:30,980
Jake, there will
always be stories,

175
00:20:30,980 --> 00:20:33,942
but you have only one family.

176
00:20:39,364 --> 00:20:41,074
The Ministry will say
no comment,

177
00:20:41,074 --> 00:20:42,617
so you'll just need
to bluff a little.

178
00:20:42,617 --> 00:20:43,702
I see.

179
00:20:43,702 --> 00:20:45,161
Make them think
that you already have

180
00:20:45,161 --> 00:20:46,413
proof of the location.

181
00:20:46,413 --> 00:20:48,373
You just need confirmation.

182
00:20:48,373 --> 00:20:49,916
But don't say the name.

183
00:20:49,916 --> 00:20:51,710
- Okay.
- Okay?

184
00:20:51,710 --> 00:20:54,129
Jake-san,
thank you for this tip.

185
00:20:54,129 --> 00:20:56,881
We gotta look out
for each other, right?

186
00:20:56,881 --> 00:20:58,508
You got this.

187
00:20:58,508 --> 00:21:05,598
<i>♪ ♪</i>

188
00:21:12,063 --> 00:21:15,066
<i>[bright music playing]</i>

189
00:21:15,066 --> 00:21:18,028
<i>♪ ♪</i>

190
00:21:18,028 --> 00:21:21,114
<i>[singing in Japanese]</i>

191
00:21:43,928 --> 00:21:45,180
Ah?

192
00:22:20,340 --> 00:22:23,259
[laughs]

193
00:22:29,057 --> 00:22:30,100
<i>Oi.</i>

194
00:22:33,520 --> 00:22:34,813
<i>[music stops]</i>

195
00:22:34,813 --> 00:22:38,817
[baby crying]

196
00:22:58,878 --> 00:23:00,588
[speaking Japanese]

197
00:23:28,366 --> 00:23:31,286
<i>[tense music]</i>

198
00:23:31,286 --> 00:23:38,376
<i>♪ ♪</i>

199
00:23:44,716 --> 00:23:47,385
[door slams]
[lock clicks]

200
00:24:02,233 --> 00:24:05,236
[both speaking Japanese]

201
00:24:11,659 --> 00:24:12,952
[sighs]

202
00:24:38,436 --> 00:24:41,439
<i>♪ ♪</i>

203
00:24:44,275 --> 00:24:51,282
<i>♪ ♪</i>

204
00:25:31,823 --> 00:25:33,533
- Are you serious?
- Huh?

205
00:25:36,161 --> 00:25:37,495
We are taking them out.

206
00:25:50,175 --> 00:25:51,760
[clears throat]

207
00:26:07,192 --> 00:26:09,319
It was temporary.

208
00:26:09,319 --> 00:26:11,196
It doesn't matter.

209
00:26:11,196 --> 00:26:15,825
It isn't really my club,
as you made perfectly clear.

210
00:26:20,372 --> 00:26:22,624
No, no,
it's actually two circles

211
00:26:22,624 --> 00:26:24,709
going in opposite directions.

212
00:26:24,709 --> 00:26:27,629
So let me get this straight.

213
00:26:27,629 --> 00:26:30,215
You're talking about
the Yamanote Line

214
00:26:30,215 --> 00:26:33,677
that makes the big circle
around Tokyo.

215
00:26:33,677 --> 00:26:35,428
Yes.

216
00:26:38,640 --> 00:26:41,476
The outer track runs clockwise,

217
00:26:41,476 --> 00:26:44,813
the inner track
counterclockwise.

218
00:26:44,813 --> 00:26:47,399
So if you prefer foreign men,

219
00:26:47,399 --> 00:26:49,943
we say you ride
the outer track.

220
00:26:49,943 --> 00:26:52,779
So I'm a foreign man.

221
00:26:52,779 --> 00:26:54,489
Well...

222
00:26:54,489 --> 00:26:56,991
[both laugh]

223
00:26:56,991 --> 00:27:00,787
And if you stick
to native Japanese men,

224
00:27:00,787 --> 00:27:03,248
you ride the inner track, right?

225
00:27:04,582 --> 00:27:08,420
[both speaking Japanese]

226
00:27:13,091 --> 00:27:17,095
So I guess
you're a outer track man, huh?

227
00:27:20,306 --> 00:27:23,059
Actually,

228
00:27:23,059 --> 00:27:26,938
tonight was my first time
on that track.

229
00:27:26,938 --> 00:27:28,481
Really?

230
00:27:32,444 --> 00:27:35,113
Thank you.

231
00:27:38,783 --> 00:27:41,619
What about you?

232
00:27:41,619 --> 00:27:43,788
To be honest,

233
00:27:43,788 --> 00:27:47,959
it's been a year
since I've been with anyone.

234
00:27:49,294 --> 00:27:50,795
Really?

235
00:27:50,795 --> 00:27:52,339
Why?

236
00:27:52,339 --> 00:27:55,633
I got tired of not liking
the people in my bed.

237
00:27:57,844 --> 00:27:59,471
Thank you.

238
00:28:05,143 --> 00:28:09,314
It was a big deal for me
to approach you at that party.

239
00:28:12,359 --> 00:28:15,945
I haven't done that
in a long time.

240
00:28:22,577 --> 00:28:26,998
You have a lot of lost time
to make up for.

241
00:28:27,999 --> 00:28:29,501
If you can keep up.

242
00:28:29,501 --> 00:28:32,504
<i>[soft music]</i>

243
00:28:32,504 --> 00:28:39,636
<i>♪ ♪</i>

244
00:28:41,680 --> 00:28:44,599
[both moaning]

245
00:28:44,599 --> 00:28:51,690
<i>♪ ♪</i>

246
00:28:58,029 --> 00:29:01,032
[both breathing heavily]

247
00:29:03,034 --> 00:29:04,577
[laughs]

248
00:29:10,542 --> 00:29:13,503
<i>[tense music]</i>

249
00:29:13,503 --> 00:29:20,593
<i>♪ ♪</i>

250
00:29:27,726 --> 00:29:30,812
[lock rattling]

251
00:29:30,812 --> 00:29:32,439
[lock clicks]

252
00:29:37,986 --> 00:29:45,035
<i>♪ ♪</i>

253
00:30:12,937 --> 00:30:16,608
So here's
Tozawa's file, right?

254
00:30:16,608 --> 00:30:19,944
And here are the files
of four other Yaks.

255
00:30:19,944 --> 00:30:22,197
Are you sure they're Yakuza?

256
00:30:22,197 --> 00:30:24,199
Dude, you know
how many fanzines I read.

257
00:30:24,199 --> 00:30:25,825
I know all their names.

258
00:30:33,625 --> 00:30:35,418
Illness of the trade.

259
00:30:35,418 --> 00:30:37,879
We call it shokugoyo.

260
00:30:37,879 --> 00:30:39,798
Yakuza live a life
filled with alcohol,

261
00:30:39,798 --> 00:30:41,800
shabu, and tattoo needles.

262
00:30:41,800 --> 00:30:44,552
Do that long enough
and you get liver disease.

263
00:30:44,552 --> 00:30:47,138
Well, it seems
Tozawa has it--

264
00:30:47,138 --> 00:30:48,139
or did.

265
00:30:48,139 --> 00:30:50,392
It's not something
they get over.

266
00:30:58,650 --> 00:31:01,653
<i>[speaking Japanese]</i>

267
00:31:13,164 --> 00:31:14,749
[speaking Japanese

268
00:31:51,953 --> 00:31:53,538
[speaking Japanese

269
00:32:15,935 --> 00:32:16,978
Hayama.

270
00:32:21,900 --> 00:32:23,234
